# Build outputs and machine state. None of this is source: it is produced by CI, by the
# media builders, or by a benchmark run, and tracking it made the repo carry megabytes of
# binaries and per-run evidence that go stale the moment anything is rebuilt.
*.obj
*.pdb
*.pfx
*.swp

# CI artifacts downloaded for local use / release assembly
artifacts/
artifacts-*/
rel-out/
release-assets/
dl/

# Per-run evidence and measurements
evidence/
# The whole scratchpad is LOCAL-ONLY (owner decision 2026-08-10): working scripts,
# drafts and run outputs stay on this machine and are never pushed.
scratchpad/
shots*.tar
*.iso
*.img

# Vendored read-only upstream checkouts
upstream/ro/
tools/*/x64/

# --- dom0 desktop captures: NEVER commit these ---------------------------------------
# `qtest fullshot` captures the WHOLE dom0 screen, other qubes included - the service's own
# installer says so. Per-window `qtest shot` output (guest windows only) is a different risk class
# and is allowed, but anything full-desktop is not.
*fullshot*
*-full/screen.png
**/fullshot/
screen.png
evidence/

# Build OUTPUT, produced by CI (release-package.yml). Never commit it: a committed copy silently
# drifted from source and shipped a pre-fix installer for three releases. See the README there.
release-artifacts/*
!release-artifacts/README.md
__pycache__/
